Runs the webtiles binary on Windows, for the native app (native/, engine.rs):
Windows has no Unix datagram sockets, so the webtiles channel is the
process's stdin and stdout there. Each control message is one line of JSON
on stdin; each flush of output goes to stdout as the socket would carry it.
tileweb.cc keeps them in the same message queue the WebAssembly build has
(wasm/bridge.h's names; WEBTILES_QUEUE), so the waits are the same. A
`hangup` control message, or the end of stdin, is a server's SIGHUP: the
game saves and exits. libw32c.cc gets the headless mode libunix.cc has (no
console; the screen in memory; keys from the webtiles channel), and main.cc
skips the UTF-8 locale check, which needs nl_langinfo.

Everything is under TARGET_OS_WINDOWS (or WEBTILES_QUEUE, which is
__EMSCRIPTEN__ elsewhere): the Linux and WebAssembly builds are unchanged.
Applies after 01-12. GPLv2+, as the files it patches.

